<title>USA: Washington Post Co Q4 shr increases.</title>
<headline>Washington Post Co Q4 shr increases.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-01-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>1996			1995</p>
<p> Shr			  $5.96		    $4.80</p>
<p> Net			 65,266		   52,890</p>
<p> Revs		     503,648		  462,986</p>
<p> Avg shrs		  10,953		   11,020</p>
<p>	  12 MONTHS</p>
<p> Shr			 $20.05		   $17.15</p>
<p> Net			220,817		  190,096</p>
<p> Revs		   1,853,445		1,719,449</p>
<p> Avg shrs		  10,980		   11,086</p>
<p>(All data above 000s except per share numbers)</p>
<p>NOTE - 1995 net income included a gain of $8.4 million, or $0.75 per share, from the sale of its investment in American PCS LP, and an after-tax charge of $5.6 million, or $0.51 per share, related to the write-off of its investment in Mammoth Micro Productions.</p>
<p>((-- New York newsdesk 212-859-1610))</p>
